{%- from "brand.njk" import img with context -%}
{#
  Cook View, set in the app's own cooking voice: the headline is Charter, like the
  step on a Cook View page. The main picture is the campaign's iPhone Duo folded
  like a laptop (App Store frame 05's pose) with Cook View on it, the step standing
  and the controls lying; beside it the campaign's dark iPhone with the same recipe
  and its timer running. The Duo's display is the first frame of FlavorDraft's real
  page turn (two seconds of the iPhone Duo film: step 16 at rest, Next pressed, the
  recorded turn, step 17), cut to the display by scripts/build-media.mjs. home.js
  lays that clip over the display's two halves, each at the plane the render
  recorded for it (scripts/screens.json, `quads`), and lets it run on its own
  while the section is in view: a hold, the turn, a hold on step 17, a dissolve
  back. Nothing needs pressing; a text control under the device pauses it, as the
  film's does. Under reduced motion, or without the script, the device simply
  holds step 16.
#}
<section class="cook" aria-labelledby="cook-title">
  <div class="wrap cook__grid">
    <div class="cook__copy">
      <h2 class="cook__title" id="cook-title">Cook <span class="nowrap">one step</span> <span class="nowrap">at a time.</span></h2>
      <p class="lede">In Cook View every step gets a page of its own, set large enough to read from across the counter. Tap Next and the page turns. A step’s timer keeps running while you get on with the next one.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cook__stage">
      <figure class="cook__duo" data-turn data-turn-quads="{{ screens['cook-duo'].quads | dump }}">
        <div class="cook__device">
          {{ img("cook-duo", "Cook View on iPhone Duo, folded like a laptop on the counter: on the standing half, the lasagna recipe’s step 16 of 20, “Repeat layering: ragu, cheese sauce, parmesan, lasagna sheets, until you have three layers. Finish with a fourth layer of lasagna sheets and pour over the remaining cheese sauce.” On the lying half, Previous, No timer and Next. Tapping Next turns the page to step 17, “Sprinkle mozzarella and any remaining parmesan on top.”", "(min-width: 90rem) 548px, (min-width: 62em) 38vw, 68vw", { class: "cook__still" }) }}
          <canvas class="cook__page cook__page--top" width="660" height="469" aria-hidden="true" data-turn-half="top"></canvas>
          <canvas class="cook__page cook__page--bottom" width="660" height="469" aria-hidden="true" data-turn-half="bottom"></canvas>
          <video class="cook__video" muted playsinline preload="none" width="660" height="938" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-turn-video>
            <source src="/assets/media/cook/cook-turn.h264.mp4" type="video/mp4">
            <source src="/assets/media/cook/cook-turn.vp9.webm" type="video/webm">
          </video>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="caption cook__caption">
          <span>On <span class="nowrap">iPhone Duo</span>, folded like a laptop: the step above, the controls below, and the page turns.</span>
          <button class="text-button" type="button" hidden data-turn-toggle>Pause the page turn</button>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="cook__iphone">
        {{ img("cook-iphone", "Cook View on iPhone: “Bake for 25 minutes or until golden and bubbling.” Page 18 of 20, with the step’s timer running at 23:10 above Previous and Next.", "(min-width: 90rem) 200px, (min-width: 62em) 14vw, 25vw") }}
        <figcaption class="caption">On iPhone, its timer running.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
